      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The test verifies that `Md5Crypt.md5Crypt(byte[])` zeroes out the input array after hashing (a security property). I'll improve understandability by:\n- Removing unused imports\n- Adding a clear Arrange / Act / Assert structure\n- Renaming the magic constant `200` and clarifying intent with a meaningful variable name\n- Replacing `new byte[buffer.length]` with an explicit `expectedZeroedBuffer` variable so the assertion reads like a sentenceNow I'll compile-check the file.The improved test compiled successfully — the refactored `Md5CryptTest_testZeroOutInput.java` is syntactically correct and all symbols resolve against the CUT."
